From b90db2ef7e79389c5d3c5f685e7abd005f1725ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:37:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: ignore sink requests from IRQ_HPD while the link
 is down

With the HPD events coming from the USB-C altmode, an IRQ_HPD can arrive
while the link is down. A monitor attached at boot sends one when the
boot mode is turned off before the next mode is set: it reports
LINK_STATUS_UPDATED after losing the link. Link maintenance then starts
with push_idle, which writes the link registers while the link clocks
are off, and the CPU hangs on the bus.

Only act on sink requests once the link is up; the link is trained from
scratch when the stream is enabled.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 5771b1805..1dc6caad7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -446,6 +446,9 @@ static int msm_dp_display_handle_irq_hpd(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "%d\n", sink_request);
 
+	if (!dp->msm_dp_display.link_ready)
+		return 0;
+
 	msm_dp_ctrl_handle_sink_request(dp->ctrl, dp->panel);
 
 	if (sink_request & DP_TEST_LINK_VIDEO_PATTERN)
-- 
